# ── CAT 01: PRAYER FORMATION (50) ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# Coming IN: 25 · Coming OUT: 25
CAT01 = [
  # COMING INTO CHRISTMAS — Prayer Formation (25)
  ("Advent Prayer","The Longest Prayer of the Year","A 4-Week Advent Series on Praying the Nativity — Using Luke 1-2 as a Complete Prayer Curriculum","The most formation-rich prayers in Scripture are inside the nativity narrative. This campaign teaches the congregation to pray them.","4 Weeks","Luke 1-2 · Psalm 40"),
  ("21-Day","Come Lord Jesus — 21 Days of Advent Prayer","The Formation Campaign That Teaches the Congregation the Church's Oldest and Most Formation-Rich Prayer","Maranatha. Two words. The first Christian prayer. The last prayer of the Bible. Twenty-one days learning to mean it.","21 Days","Revelation 22:20 · 1 Corinthians 16:22"),
  ("7-Day","The Magnificat as Prayer","7 Days Praying Mary's Song Line by Line — The Most Theologically Dense Advent Prayer Ever Spoken","He has scattered the proud. He has brought down rulers. He has filled the hungry. Seven days praying the most radical prayer of the Christmas season.","7 Days","Luke 1:46-55"),
  ("40-Day","Praying the Prophecies","40 Days of Praying the Messianic Prophecies Before They Are Fulfilled at the Manger","Forty days. One Messianic prophecy per day. Prayed back to God as an act of expectancy before Christmas arrives.","40 Days","Isaiah 1-66 · Micah · Malachi"),
  ("4-Week","The Benedictus Formation","4 Weeks on Zechariah's Song — The Prayer of the Priest Who Could Not Speak for Nine Months","He was struck mute. He pondered for nine months. When he opened his mouth, this prayer came out. The formation of the congregation that has been waiting long enough to pray from depth.","4 Weeks","Luke 1:67-79"),
  ("3-Week","Advent Intercession","3 Weeks of Formation in Corporate Intercession — The Congregation That Prays Christmas Into Its City","The congregation that intercedes for its city in Advent carries the announcement differently on Christmas Eve.","3 Weeks","Isaiah 62:6-7 · Luke 2:10"),
  ("21-Day","The Nunc Dimittis Life","21 Days on Simeon's Prayer — The Formation of the Person Who Prays Lord Now Let Your Servant Depart","Lord, now you are letting your servant depart in peace. The prayer that can only be prayed by someone who has received what they were waiting for.","21 Days","Luke 2:29-32 · Philippians 1:21"),
  ("4-Week","Anna's Prayer — The Formation of the Night-and-Day Intercessor","4 Weeks on the Prayer Life That Produces the Person Who Recognizes the Messiah When He Arrives","She fasted and prayed night and day. When the baby arrived, she recognized him. The formation connection between prayer and perception.","4 Weeks","Luke 2:36-38 · 1 Thessalonians 5:17"),
  ("7-Day","The Seven Advent Prayers","7 Days — One Classic Advent Prayer Per Day — From Augustine to Barth","Seven prayers. Seven centuries. Seven theologians who prayed their way to Christmas with more depth than we usually manage.","7 Days","Various · Luke 1-2"),
  ("40-Day","The Lord's Prayer in Advent","40 Days of Advent Formation Using the Lord's Prayer as the Architecture","Your kingdom come. Your will be done on earth as in heaven. Forty days praying the Lord's Prayer into every dimension of Advent preparation.","40 Days","Matthew 6:9-13 · Luke 11:2-4"),
  ("3-Week","The Prayer That Prepared the Way","3 Weeks on John the Baptist's Formation Through Desert Prayer Before His Public Ministry","He was in the wilderness until the day of his public appearance. The formation that happens in the wilderness of prayer before the announcement.","3 Weeks","Luke 1:80 · Isaiah 40:3"),
  ("21-Day","Advent Lament — The Prayers God Answers With a Baby","21 Days on the Formation of the Congregation That Brings Its Grief to God in Advent","Barren women. Widows. Exiles. Prisoners. God answered every one of them with a child. The Advent prayer that is honest about the darkness.","21 Days","Luke 1:13 · Psalm 113:9 · Isaiah 49:15"),
  ("4-Week","The Prayer of Expectation","4 Weeks on What It Means to Pray With Advent Expectancy — Not Hope in General but Specific, Named Hope","Simeon did not pray Lord do something. He prayed Lord let me see the consolation of Israel. Specific. Named. Expected. The formation of specific Advent prayer.","4 Weeks","Luke 2:25-26 · Habakkuk 2:1"),
  ("6-Week","From Darkness to the Doxology","6 Weeks of Prayer Formation — Beginning With Lament and Arriving at Worship on Christmas Eve","Week 1: Psalm 88. Week 2: Lamentations 3. Week 3: Isaiah 64. Week 4: Hannah. Week 5: Magnificat. Week 6: Gloria. Six weeks from the deepest lament to the highest worship.","6 Weeks","Psalms 88 · Luke 1:46 · 2:14"),
  ("21-Day","Praying for the Unchurched Before Christmas Eve","21 Days of Formation in Intercession for the People Who Will Come to Christmas Eve","The congregation that has been praying for specific people by name for twenty-one days arrives at Christmas Eve differently.","21 Days","1 Timothy 2:1-4 · Luke 15:4-7"),
  ("3-Week","The Gabriel Prayer — When God Answers With More Than You Asked","3 Weeks on the Prayers That Were Answered at the Incarnation — Zechariah's, Mary's, Elizabeth's","He prayed for a son. God gave him the forerunner of the Messiah. She asked how this would happen. God gave her the Son. The Advent theology of the answered prayer that exceeds the request.","3 Weeks","Luke 1:13-17 · Ephesians 3:20"),
  ("40-Day","Praying the Psalms Through Advent","40 Days of Advent Prayer Formed by the Psalter — One Psalm Per Day From Darkness to Praise","From Psalm 88 to Psalm 150. The Psalter is the prayer book of the incarnation. The congregation that prays it in Advent arrives at Christmas formed.","40 Days","Psalms 1-150"),
  ("7-Day","Seven Days of Fasting and Prayer Before Christmas","The Formation Campaign for the Final Week of Advent — Fasting Before the Feast","You cannot receive the feast if you have not fasted. Seven days before Christmas. One day of fasting and prayer per day. The formation that prepares the body to receive the announcement.","7 Days","Matthew 6:16-18 · Luke 1:53"),
  ("4-Week","The Visitation Prayer","4 Weeks on Mary's Visit to Elizabeth — What Happens When Two Praying Women Meet","When Elizabeth heard Mary's greeting, the baby leaped and she was filled with the Holy Spirit. The formation of the community of prayer that produces that kind of encounter.","4 Weeks","Luke 1:39-45"),
  ("21-Day","The Wilderness Prayer","21 Days of Formation in the Prayer That Produces John the Baptist — The Prayer of the Wilderness","He was in the wilderness from birth. The prayer that forms in the wilderness is the prayer that can announce the Messiah in public.","21 Days","Luke 1:80 · Mark 1:2-4"),
  ("3-Week","Praying the Census — When Providence Answers Prayer in Unexpected Ways","3 Weeks on Luke 2:1 — The Formation of the Congregation That Sees God's Answer Arriving Through Caesar's Decree","Joseph and Mary prayed for the Messiah like every faithful Jew. Caesar Augustus ordered a census. The answer to their prayer used an emperor as its instrument.","3 Weeks","Luke 2:1 · Proverbs 21:1"),
  ("40-Day","The Four-Hundred-Year Prayer","40 Days on the Prayers That Were Being Prayed During the Four Centuries of Silence Between Malachi and Matthew","The formation of the congregation that prays for what it cannot yet see. Forty days in the prayers of the intertestamental period.","40 Days","Malachi 4 · Luke 1:6 · 2:25"),
  ("6-Week","Night Prayer — The Advent Formation of Praying Before Sleep","6 Weeks of Compline — The Church's Ancient Night Prayer Reclaimed for Advent Formation","The night office. The prayer before sleep. The six weeks of Advent prayed at the end of each day by a congregation that wants to wake on Christmas morning formed.","6 Weeks","Psalm 134 · Luke 2:8 · Luke 1:79"),
  ("4-Week","The Prayer That Mary Did Not Pray","4 Weeks on the Prayer Mary Did Not Pray When Gabriel Arrived — and the Prayer She Chose Instead","She could have prayed for clarity, for delay, for another option. She prayed let it be to me according to your word. The formation of the congregation that prays the same.","4 Weeks","Luke 1:38 · Matthew 26:39"),
  ("7-Day","The Advent of Prayer — 7 Days Restarting the Prayer Life Before Christmas","The Formation Campaign for the Congregation Member Who Has Stopped Praying — or Never Started","Christmas is the most natural moment to restart a prayer life. Seven days. One practice per day. The formation of the person who arrives at Christmas Eve talking to God again.","7 Days","Matthew 6:9-13 · Luke 18:1"),

  # COMING OUT OF CHRISTMAS — Prayer Formation (25)
  ("Epiphany Prayer","The Prayer That Follows the Star","A 4-Week Post-Christmas Prayer Formation Series on the Magi's Prayerful Journey","They did not know what they would find. They went anyway. The formation of the congregation that prays toward what it cannot yet see.","4 Weeks","Matthew 2:1-12 · Hebrews 11:8"),
  ("21-Day","Praying the New Year","21 Days of Post-Christmas Prayer Formation — Giving the Year to God Before You Know What It Holds","The congregation that gives the year to God in prayer before the first Monday of January enters the year differently.","21 Days","Psalm 90 · Proverbs 16:9"),
  ("7-Day","The Presentation Prayer — Simeon's Example for January","7 Days on What It Means to Bring What You Have Received at Christmas to God's Presence","He received the child. He prayed over him. He gave him back. The formation of the congregation that presents what it has received at Christmas.","7 Days","Luke 2:27-32"),
  ("40-Day","Post-Christmas Intercession","40 Days of Intercessory Formation — Carrying the Christmas Announcement Into the Year Through Prayer","The congregation that intercedes for its city for forty days after Christmas is doing what the shepherds did — they told everyone what they had seen.","40 Days","Luke 2:17-18 · Romans 10:1"),
  ("4-Week","The Post-Christmas Examen","4 Weeks of Formation in the Daily Examen — The Ignatian Prayer Practice That Carries Christmas Into Every Day","The daily examen is the most ancient practice for bringing God's presence into the ordinary day. This campaign introduces it in the post-Christmas window.","4 Weeks","Psalm 139:23-24 · 1 John 1:9"),
  ("3-Week","Praying the Ascension After Christmas","3 Weeks on the Prayer Life of the Congregation That Knows Jesus Is Currently Alive and Interceding","He lives to make intercession for us. The post-Christmas formation of the congregation that prays to a currently living, currently reigning, currently interceding Lord.","3 Weeks","Hebrews 7:25 · Romans 8:34"),
  ("21-Day","The New Year Prayer of Surrender","21 Days of Formation in the Prayer That Changes the Year — Not a Resolution but a Surrender","The most powerful New Year prayer is not Lord help me do better. It is Lord I give you this year. The formation of the congregation that prays the second prayer.","21 Days","Luke 1:38 · Matthew 6:10"),
  ("4-Week","Corporate Prayer After Christmas","4 Weeks of Formation in the Post-Christmas Acts 2 Prayer Gathering","They devoted themselves to prayer. The congregation that builds corporate prayer into the first month of the year has structured the year for formation.","4 Weeks","Acts 2:42 · Acts 4:24-31"),
  ("7-Day","Seven Prayers for the New Year","7 Classic Prayers for the Seven Dimensions of the Congregation's Formation Year","One prayer per area of life. Work. Marriage. Parenting. Money. Health. Purpose. Death. The formation of the congregation that begins the year praying across every dimension.","7 Days","Ephesians 1:17-19 · Colossians 1:9-12"),
  ("3-Week","The Prayer of Epiphany","3 Weeks on the Star — The Formation of the Congregation That Prays Toward What It Cannot Yet Fully See","They followed a star. They did not know exactly what they would find. They went anyway. The formation of the post-Christmas congregation that prays toward its calling.","3 Weeks","Matthew 2:1-12 · Hebrews 12:2"),
  ("40-Day","Praying the One Another Commands","40 Days of Post-Christmas Intercessory Formation — 40 One Another Commands as Prayers for the Community","One another. One practice per day. The congregation that prays the one another commands for forty days after Christmas has built the formation architecture for community.","40 Days","Romans 12:10 · Galatians 6:2"),
  ("21-Day","Post-Christmas Night Prayer","21 Days of Formation in Compline — The Night Office for January","The congregation that ends each day in January with the ancient night prayer arrives at February having been formed by three weeks of consistent prayer.","21 Days","Psalm 4 · Psalm 134 · Luke 2:29"),
  ("4-Week","The Post-Christmas Fast","4 Weeks of Formation in the Practice of Post-Christmas Fasting as Counterformation","The culture feasts through December and detoxes in January. The church fasts in December and feasts at Christmas. The post-Christmas fast is the continuation of the formation.","4 Weeks","Isaiah 58:6-7 · Matthew 6:16-18"),
  ("6-Week","Praying Into the Mission","6 Weeks of Post-Christmas Intercessory Formation for the Congregation's Annual Mission","The mission of the year is carried by prayer. This campaign forms the congregation in the specific intercessory practices that carry the year's mission.","6 Weeks","Colossians 4:2-4 · Acts 13:1-3"),
  ("7-Day","The Praying Church in January","7 Days of Formation in What It Means to Be a Congregation Known for Its Prayer in the New Year","The early church was known for its prayer before it was known for anything else. The formation of the congregation that recovers that reputation.","7 Days","Acts 2:42 · Acts 12:5"),
  ("21-Day","Praying Philippians in January","21 Days of Post-Christmas Prayer Formation in the Most Prayer-Dense Epistle in the New Testament","Do not be anxious about anything but in every situation by prayer and petition with thanksgiving present your requests to God. The formation of the congregation that actually does this.","21 Days","Philippians 4:6-7 · 1:9-11"),
  ("40-Day","The Prayer of Consecration","40 Days of Formation in the Post-Christmas Practice of Consecrating the Year — Presenting the Year to God","The year is a gift you have not used yet. The formation of the congregation that presents it to God before they spend it.","40 Days","Romans 12:1 · Psalm 31:15"),
  ("3-Week","Praying for Those Who Came to Christmas Eve","3 Weeks of Specific Intercessory Formation for the People Who Were in the Building on Christmas Eve","The formation of the congregation that prays for the people who came but have not been back. The prayer that carries the Christmas invitation into January.","3 Weeks","Luke 15:4 · 1 Timothy 2:1"),
  ("4-Week","Silence and Prayer in January","4 Weeks on the Formation of Silence as the Ground of Post-Christmas Prayer","The culture moves from December noise directly into January noise. The congregation that cultivates silence in January has the ground from which prayer grows.","4 Weeks","Psalm 46:10 · Habakkuk 2:20"),
  ("21-Day","Post-Christmas Psalms","21 Days of Prayer Formation in the Post-Christmas Psalms — The Psalter From Advent to Ordinary Time","The formation of the congregation that keeps praying the Psalms after the Christmas music has been put away.","21 Days","Psalms 1-21 · Colossians 3:16"),
  ("6-Week","The Year Began With Prayer","6 Weeks of Formation That Launches the Year's Formation Arc From a Prayer Foundation","Acts 13:1-3. They worshipped. They fasted. They prayed. Then they sent. The congregation that launches the year from that sequence has a different year.","6 Weeks","Acts 13:1-3 · Nehemiah 1:4"),
  ("7-Day","Praying the Epiphany","7 Days in the Epiphany Texts as Prayers — Isaiah 60, Matthew 2, John 1","The light has come. The nations are coming. The star is rising. Seven days of post-Christmas prayer from the formation texts of Epiphany.","7 Days","Isaiah 60:1-3 · Matthew 2:1-12"),
  ("40-Day","The Prayer Posture of the Year","40 Days of Formation in the Post-Christmas Physical Practices of Prayer — Kneeling, Lifting Hands, Walking, Bowing","The body is the site of formation. The congregation that forms its body in prayer for forty days after Christmas has built the formation architecture for the year.","40 Days","Philippians 2:10 · Psalm 95:6"),
  ("3-Week","Praying the Incarnation Into Your City","3 Weeks of Post-Christmas Formation in Praying the Theology of the Incarnation Into the Specific Streets, Neighborhoods, and Communities of Your City","The Word became flesh and moved into a neighborhood. The formation of the congregation that prays the incarnation into its specific neighborhood.","3 Weeks","John 1:14 · Jeremiah 29:7"),
  ("21-Day","When Prayer Becomes Formation","21 Days of Post-Christmas Teaching on What Prayer Does to the Person Who Prays It — Not Only What It Produces in the World","The formation of the congregation that understands prayer not primarily as petition but as transformation.","21 Days","Romans 8:26-27 · 2 Corinthians 3:18"),
]

# ── CAT 02: THEOLOGY OF WAITING (50) ──────────────────────────────────────────
CAT02 = [
  # COMING INTO CHRISTMAS (25)
  ("Advent","The Formation of the Four-Century Wait","A 6-Week Pre-Christmas Series on What the Four Hundred Years of Silence Between Malachi and Matthew Formed in Israel","Four hundred years. No prophet. No word. Only faithfulness to what had been given. The formation of the congregation that understands what waiting produces.","6 Weeks","Malachi 4 · Luke 1:6 · 2:25"),
  ("7-Day","Simeon's Seven Decades","7 Days on the Formation of the Man Who Waited His Entire Life for the Consolation of Israel","He had been waiting so long he was ready to die when it arrived. The formation of the congregation that waits well enough to receive what it has been promised.","7 Days","Luke 2:25-32"),
  ("40-Day","The Theology of Not Yet","40 Days of Advent Formation on the Formation That Happens in the Gap Between Promise and Fulfillment","The promise was given in Genesis 3:15. The fulfillment arrived in Luke 2. The congregation that walks the gap understands the formation that waiting produces.","40 Days","Genesis 3:15 · Galatians 4:4"),
  ("4-Week","Anna's Eighty-Four Years","4 Weeks on the Formation of the Woman Who Waited Longer Than Anyone and Recognized What Others Missed","She fasted and prayed for decades. When the answer arrived, she recognized it and could not stop talking about it. The formation that waiting produces in the one who waits well.","4 Weeks","Luke 2:36-38"),
  ("21-Day","Abraham's Twenty-Five Years","21 Days on the Formation of Abraham's Wait for the Child of Promise — and What It Has to Do With Christmas","He waited twenty-five years for Isaac. The formation of the congregation that holds the promise during the wait.","21 Days","Genesis 12:1-3 · 21:1-7 · Galatians 4:4"),
  ("3-Week","The Theology of the Advent Candles","3 Weeks on What the Gradual Lighting of the Advent Wreath Actually Teaches About the Theology of Progressive Revelation","The darkness does not go away all at once. One candle per week. The formation of the congregation that understands why God does things gradually.","3 Weeks","Isaiah 9:2 · John 1:5 · Luke 1"),
  ("4-Week","Hannah's Two Pilgrimages","4 Weeks on Hannah's Formation — The Barren Woman Who Went to Shiloh Every Year and One Year Received the Answer","She went every year. She prayed the same prayer. One year it was answered. The formation of the congregation that does not give up before the answer.","4 Weeks","1 Samuel 1:1-2:11"),
  ("40-Day","The Intertestamental Wait","40 Days on the Formation of Faithful Judaism Between Malachi and Matthew — What They Were Doing While God Was Apparently Silent","The synagogue. The Psalms. The Torah. The community. The formation of the congregation that is faithful in the silence.","40 Days","Malachi · Luke 1:6 · Acts 10:2"),
  ("21-Day","The Long Advent","21 Days on the Formation That Only Long Waiting Produces","Impatient waiting produces anxiety. Patient waiting produces formation. The formation of the congregation that learns to wait in a way that produces something.","21 Days","Isaiah 40:31 · Psalm 27:14"),
  ("7-Day","The Birth Pangs of Advent","7 Days on Romans 8 as an Advent Text — The Groaning of Creation as a Theology of Waiting for the Full Redemption","The creation waits in eager expectation. The children of God wait for the adoption. The formation of the congregation that understands its waiting as participation in something cosmic.","7 Days","Romans 8:18-25 · Luke 2:14"),
  ("4-Week","Joseph's Twelve Years in the Pit and Prison","4 Weeks on the Formation of the Man Who Waited Longest Before the Promise and Found the Purpose","The pit. The prison. The cup-bearer who forgot him. Thirteen years of waiting. The formation that produced the man who saved a nation.","4 Weeks","Genesis 37-50 · Luke 2:52"),
  ("3-Week","Zechariah's Nine Months","3 Weeks on the Formation of the Priest Who Could Not Speak for Nine Months and Emerged With the Greatest Prayer of the Nativity","He was struck silent. He pondered what no one else knew. He emerged with the Benedictus. The formation of the congregation that learns to wait in silence.","3 Weeks","Luke 1:20-25 · 1:67-79"),
  ("21-Day","Advent and the Unfulfilled Promise","21 Days of Formation for the Congregation Member Who Is Still Waiting for What God Has Promised","She is still waiting. He prayed the same prayer again. They have been faithful and have not received. The formation of the congregation that does not give up.","21 Days","Hebrews 11:13 · Habakkuk 3:17-19"),
  ("40-Day","The Prophets' Longing","40 Days on 1 Peter 1:10-12 — The Formation of Those Who Searched and Found What They Were Searching About, But Did Not See","They searched. They inquired. They investigated carefully. They were serving not themselves but you. Forty days on the formation of those who prepare the way for what they will not see arrive.","40 Days","1 Peter 1:10-12 · Matthew 13:17"),
  ("6-Week","Advent Deceleration","6 Weeks of Formation in the Countercultural Practice of Slowing Down Before Christmas","The culture accelerates in December. The church decelerates. Six weeks of practices that form the congregation to slow down enough to receive what Christmas is offering.","6 Weeks","Psalm 46:10 · Isaiah 30:15"),
  ("4-Week","The Theology of Not Having It All","4 Weeks of Advent Formation on Contentment — What the Congregation That Does Not Have Everything It Wants Has in Common With Israel at Advent","Israel did not have the Messiah yet. The congregation does not have everything it wants yet. The formation of the congregation in the theology of not yet.","4 Weeks","Philippians 4:11-12 · Romans 8:24-25"),
  ("21-Day","The Calendar as Formation Tool","21 Days on What It Means to Structure the Year Around Waiting and Receiving — The Christian Calendar as a Formation System","The Christian year is a formation curriculum. It begins with Advent because it knows that formation begins with waiting. The formation of the congregation that takes the calendar seriously.","21 Days","Galatians 4:4 · Ecclesiastes 3:1"),
  ("3-Week","The Widow's Advent","3 Weeks on the Widows of the Nativity — Anna, and the Formation of Those Who Wait With Nothing Left But God","She had lost her husband. She had no children. She had only the temple and the prayer. She was there when the answer arrived. The formation of the person who has been reduced to God alone.","3 Weeks","Luke 2:36-38 · Psalm 146:9"),
  ("7-Day","The Formation of Expectancy","7 Days on the Difference Between Mere Waiting and Active Expectation — The Formation of Advent Alertness","He who is coming will come and will not delay. The formation of the congregation that waits the way a watchman watches — alert, attentive, expecting.","7 Days","Habakkuk 2:3 · Luke 12:35-40"),
  ("40-Day","Advent as Recapitulation","40 Days on the Theology of the Christian Calendar — Why the Church Lives the Wait Every Year as Formation","You do not wait for the Messiah annually because you have forgotten he came. You wait annually because waiting forms you. The formation of the congregation that understands recapitulation.","40 Days","Romans 15:4 · 1 Corinthians 10:11"),
  ("4-Week","The Patience of the Farmer","4 Weeks on James 5:7-8 as an Advent Text — The Farmer Who Waits for the Autumn and Spring Rains","Be patient, therefore, brothers and sisters, until the coming of the Lord. See how the farmer waits. The formation of the congregation that waits with the patience of those who understand seasons.","4 Weeks","James 5:7-8 · Psalm 126:5-6"),
  ("21-Day","The Formation of Holy Longing","21 Days on the Theology of Desire in Advent — What It Means to Long for What You Do Not Yet Have","Blessed are those who hunger and thirst. The formation of the congregation that learns to long well — specifically, expectantly, persistently.","21 Days","Matthew 5:6 · Psalm 63:1 · Isaiah 55:1"),
  ("6-Week","The Sunday of Hope","6 Weeks Beginning With the First Sunday of Advent — The Formation of a Congregation Around the Specific, Named Hope of the Incarnation","Hope. Not optimism. Not wishful thinking. Named. Specific. Grounded. The formation of a congregation that hopes the way Scripture teaches hoping.","6 Weeks","Romans 5:1-5 · Luke 1:46-55"),
  ("3-Week","Advent for the Impatient","3 Weeks of Formation for the Congregation Member Who Cannot Wait — Who Wants the Answer Now","He who is coming will come and will not delay. But he has not come yet. The formation of the congregation that learns to stay in the Advent season without rushing to Christmas.","3 Weeks","Habakkuk 2:3 · Romans 8:25"),
  ("7-Day","The Children of Promise","7 Days on Isaac, Samuel, John the Baptist, and Jesus — The Four Children of Promise and What Their Births Say About Waiting","Each was promised before he was conceived. Each required a wait that seemed impossible. Each arrived at exactly the right moment. The formation of the congregation around the theology of the promised child.","7 Days","Genesis 21 · 1 Samuel 1 · Luke 1"),

  # COMING OUT OF CHRISTMAS (25)
  ("Post-Christmas","The End of the Wait — And What Comes After","A 4-Week Post-Christmas Series on What the Formation of Waiting Produces in Those Who Receive What They Were Waiting For","Simeon received the child and was ready to die in peace. The formation of the congregation that has received Christmas and is now ready for what comes next.","4 Weeks","Luke 2:29-32 · Philippians 1:21"),
  ("7-Day","The Day After the Stable","7 Days on What the Shepherds Did the Morning After Christmas — And What the Formation of Receiving Looks Like","They returned, glorifying and praising God for all the things they had heard and seen. The formation of the congregation that knows what to do with what it has received.","7 Days","Luke 2:20 · 1 Thessalonians 5:16-18"),
  ("21-Day","The Wait That Is Still Waiting","21 Days of Post-Christmas Formation on the Return of Christ — The Advent That Is Not Yet Completed","He came once. He is coming again. The formation of the congregation that holds both comings together — celebrating the first while waiting for the second.","21 Days","Revelation 22:20 · 1 Thessalonians 4:16"),
  ("40-Day","The Post-Christmas Pilgrimage","40 Days of Formation in the Journey From Christmas to Easter — The Formation of the Congregation That Lives Between the Two","Christmas and Easter are the two poles of the Christian year. The forty days after Christmas are the beginning of the journey toward the cross and resurrection.","40 Days","Luke 2:22-52 · John 1:14-18"),
  ("4-Week","The Patience of January","4 Weeks of Post-Christmas Formation in the Virtue of Patience — The Most Undervalued Formation Outcome of the Christmas Season","The congregation that has waited through Advent has been formed in patience. This campaign extends that formation into the year.","4 Weeks","James 1:3-4 · Romans 5:3-5"),
  ("3-Week","The Long View","3 Weeks of Post-Christmas Formation in the Eschatological Patience That Christmas Grounds","Christmas is not the end of the story. It is the beginning of the last chapter. The formation of the congregation that holds the long view.","3 Weeks","2 Peter 3:8-9 · Revelation 21:5"),
  ("21-Day","The Hidden Years","21 Days on What Jesus Was Doing Between the Manger and the Jordan — The Formation of Patient Hiddenness","He increased in wisdom and stature and in favor with God and man. Thirty years. One sentence. The formation of the congregation that understands hiddenness as formation.","21 Days","Luke 2:40-52"),
  ("4-Week","The Feast After the Fast","4 Weeks on the Post-Christmas Formation of the Congregation That Has Waited Well and Now Receives Well","The congregation that fasted in Advent feasts at Christmas. The feasting is the formation of gratitude. The post-Christmas campaign that forms gratitude from the Christmas received.","4 Weeks","Luke 14:15-24 · Psalm 34:8"),
  ("7-Day","From Manger to Mission","7 Days on the Formation Arc From Christmas to the Great Commission — The Journey From Receiving to Sending","He was born to a couple who had nowhere to sleep. He grew up. He was sent. He sent others. The post-Christmas formation of the sent congregation.","7 Days","Luke 2:7 · John 20:21 · Acts 1:8"),
  ("3-Week","The Congregation Still Waiting","3 Weeks of Post-Christmas Formation for the Congregation Member Who Expected Christmas to Change More Than It Did","She attended Christmas Eve. She went home. Everything was the same. The formation of the congregation that understands formation is not always immediate.","3 Weeks","Romans 5:3-5 · 2 Corinthians 4:17"),
  ("40-Day","The Formation of Hope After Christmas","40 Days of Post-Christmas Formation in the Hope That the Incarnation Grounds — Not Optimism, But Certainty","The resurrection is the ground of hope. The incarnation is the beginning of the ground. The post-Christmas formation of the congregation in grounded, specific, named hope.","40 Days","Romans 5:1-5 · 1 Peter 1:3-5"),
  ("21-Day","Contentment After Christmas","21 Days of Post-Christmas Formation in the Theology of Contentment — What Having Received What Matters Most Does to the Person Who Holds Everything Else Loosely","He became poor so that we might become rich. Having received that richness, the post-Christmas formation of the congregation in contentment with everything else.","21 Days","Philippians 4:11-13 · 1 Timothy 6:6"),
  ("6-Week","The Epiphany of Waiting","6 Weeks of Post-Christmas Formation in the Theology of Expectation — What Christmas Revealed About What Is Still Coming","Christmas revealed the nature of God's coming. It did not reveal all of it. The formation of the congregation that lives in the light of what has been revealed while expecting more.","6 Weeks","1 Corinthians 13:12 · Revelation 21-22"),
  ("4-Week","The January Deceleration","4 Weeks of Post-Christmas Formation in the Practice of Not Rushing Past What Christmas Has Produced","The culture moves at maximum velocity from December 26 onward. The church sits with what it has received. The formation of the congregation that decelerates in January.","4 Weeks","Psalm 46:10 · Luke 2:19"),
  ("21-Day","The Formation of Gratitude","21 Days of Post-Christmas Formation in Gratitude as the Primary Response to Christmas","Twenty-one days. One dimension of gratitude per day. The formation of the congregation that does not move past Christmas without sitting in what it has been given.","21 Days","1 Thessalonians 5:18 · Psalm 100"),
  ("7-Day","Seven Things Christmas Did Not Fix","7 Days of Post-Christmas Honest Formation — What the Incarnation Is and Is Not the Answer To","Christmas is not the answer to everything yet. Some things wait for Easter. Some things wait for the Parousia. The formation of the congregation that holds the tension.","7 Days","Romans 8:22-25 · Revelation 21:4"),
  ("3-Week","The Formation of Receiving","3 Weeks on What It Means to Actually Receive What Christmas Offered","John 1:12 — to all who received him. The formation of the congregation that distinguishes between attending Christmas and receiving Christmas.","3 Weeks","John 1:12 · Acts 2:38"),
  ("40-Day","Post-Christmas Waiting for Easter","40 Days of Formation in the Journey Between the Incarnation and the Atonement — Living in What Christmas Started Toward What Easter Completed","Christmas and Easter are one movement. The forty days after Christmas are the beginning of the formation arc toward Good Friday and Easter.","40 Days","Luke 2:34-35 · Isaiah 53:4-6"),
  ("4-Week","The Patient Congregation","4 Weeks on What It Looks Like for a Congregation to Wait Well in January — When the Feeling Has Faded and the Formation Must Be Sustained","January is the formation test. The congregation that persists in formation when the feeling is gone has been formed in the deepest sense.","4 Weeks","Galatians 6:9 · Hebrews 12:1"),
  ("21-Day","The New Year and the Second Advent","21 Days of Post-Christmas Formation in the Eschatological Hope That Reorganizes the New Year","He came. He is coming again. The formation of the congregation that begins the new year with the second Advent as its horizon.","21 Days","1 Thessalonians 4:16-18 · Titus 2:13"),
  ("6-Week","From Bethlehem to the New Jerusalem","6 Weeks of Post-Christmas Eschatological Formation — Reading Christmas as the Beginning of the Story That Ends in Revelation 21","The manger is the beginning. The new Jerusalem is the end. The formation of the congregation that holds the whole story.","6 Weeks","Luke 2:7 · Revelation 21:1-5"),
  ("7-Day","Seven Dimensions of What Christmas Changed","7 Days of Post-Christmas Formation — What the Incarnation Changed About Your Identity, Purpose, Relationships, Work, Money, Death, and Future","One dimension per day. The congregation that completes this week has been formed in the full scope of what Christmas changed.","7 Days","2 Corinthians 5:17 · Ephesians 1:3-14"),
  ("40-Day","The Long Formation","40 Days of Post-Christmas Formation in the Understanding That Formation Is Always Longer Than the Feeling","The feeling of Christmas lasts three days. The formation of Christmas lasts a lifetime. The congregation that understands the difference is the congregation that stays with the formation.","40 Days","Philippians 1:6 · Romans 8:29"),
  ("3-Week","Holding Christmas Longer","3 Weeks of Formation in the Practice of Sitting With Christmas Until It Has Done Its Work","The congregation that holds Christmas longer than December produces formation. The congregation that moves past it on December 26 receives inspiration.","3 Weeks","Luke 2:19 · Psalm 1:2"),
  ("21-Day","After Simeon — Carrying What You Have Been Given","21 Days of Post-Christmas Formation for the Congregation That Has Received the Gift and Now Must Carry It","He received the child. He prayed. He gave him back. But the word he spoke to Mary stayed with her for thirty years. The formation of the congregation that carries what Christmas has given.","21 Days","Luke 2:34-35 · Galatians 2:20"),
]
